# Flutter / Riverpod

State management status: The codebase currently uses StatefulWidget; flutter_riverpod is not yet in pubspec.yaml. Use Riverpod for NEW features and for screens that must change substantially anyway; add the dependency when the first such feature is implemented (user approved). Do NOT mass-migrate existing screens. Match the existing StatefulWidget style elsewhere.

Before writing code: check `pubspec.yaml` for the Riverpod version and whether `riverpod_generator` is used. Follow the EXISTING style in neighboring files. Do not mix generated and hand-written providers in one feature.

## Riverpod
- New code: prefer `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier`. Do not introduce legacy `StateNotifier`, `StateProvider` or `ChangeNotifier` unless the surrounding code already uses it.
- `ref.watch` only in `build` / provider bodies. `ref.read` in callbacks. `ref.listen` for side effects (navigation, snackbars). Never `ref.watch` inside callbacks.
- All Supabase calls (RPC, Edge Function, queries) live in repository providers, never in widgets.
- Always handle all `AsyncValue` states (loading, error, data). Surface errors to the user; never swallow them.
- Keep providers small and autoDispose by default; keep alive only when state must persist.

## Widgets / UI
- No business logic or state transitions in widgets. Widgets render state and dispatch intents.
- Check `context.mounted` after every `await` before using `BuildContext`.
- Do not change existing UI layout, theme or navigation unless the task requires it.
- Flutter Web is a target: avoid `dart:io`; use platform-safe APIs.
- Do not add a package unless clearly needed; if you do, say why and pick a maintained one.
- Task-completion long-press (4s) is presentation only. Send the completion request to the server and render the server result.
- Long-press UX guards: issue idempotency key at hold start, memory only (never persist). Reset progress to 0 immediately on release, cancel, or app background. Only one hold at a time. Block starting a hold when under 5s to deadline (UX only; server time is authoritative). Provide a confirm-dialog alternative for screen readers (same complete-task call).

## Tests
- Test providers/notifiers with `ProviderContainer` and `overrides`; fake the repository. Never hit a real Supabase in unit tests.
- Add or update a test for each behavior change. Keep tests deterministic (no real timers; use fake async).
- Follow the `verification` skill for commands.
